---
source: tests/steps/l01_05_lexer_strings/holes.rs
expression: "out.join(\"\\n\")"
---
"\"${name\""
    [7..8] malformed string: the string is not closed
"\"${x // c}\""
    [5..11] malformed string: a `//` comment in a hole of a `"` string runs to the end of the line, past the `}`; write `/* … */`
"\"${x\n}\""
    [1..4] malformed string: a hole in a `"` string closes on its line
"\"${\"inner}\""
    [1..11] malformed string: the `${` hole is not closed
"\"${x /* open }\""
    [5..15] the block comment is not closed (1 `*/` missing)
"\"\"\"\n  ${x}\n    \"\"\""
    [4..6] malformed string: this line is indented less than the closing `"""`
